sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Morphogenetic problem-solving cases indicate that anatomical development is not entirely open-loop: large-scale feedback loops measure distance from a target anatomical state and execute diverse molecular steps to reduce the error, and such networks can store setpoints that are complex data structures rather than simple scalars.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Anatomical homeostasis uses large-scale feedback loops that reduce error from a target";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “The Collective Intelligence of Cell Groups › The Competencies of Anatomical Homeostasis”. Scope: Regulative development and regeneration in animals (e.g. the cases in the paper's Table 1)"
}
